            <div xml:id="d342">

                <pb facs="0518" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg476"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 20, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In a note which you did Mr. Stuart the
                    honor to write to him on the 23d of October last, you were so good as to say
                    that the case of the British schooner Will-of-the-wisp should be taken into
                    early consideration. One of the members of the firm of Salter &amp; Twining, of
                    Halifax, called upon me the day before yesterday, and informed me that the
                    interests of the firm were suffering from the delay in bringing the case to a
                    settlement. I venture, therefore to press upon the immediate attention of the
                    government of the United States the representation concerning the
                    Will-of-the-wisp, which was addressed to you by Mr. Stuart on the 20th October
                    last, in pursuance of instructions from her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
